# ZAS³ asset credits
#
# Every file under a project's src/<set>/resources/assets/ directory has one
# entry here (NFR-045). All assets are licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 International;
# see LICENSE-ASSETS. scripts/check_credits.py checks this file in CI.
#
# Format
#
# An entry is a block of "key: value" lines. Blank lines separate entries.
# Lines starting with "#" are comments. Each entry starts with "path", the
# file's path from the repository root, with forward slashes, followed by
# "origin": original, vgstation13 or other.
#
# An asset drawn from scratch for ZAS³:
#
#   path: zas/src/main/resources/assets/zas/textures/item/gauge.png
#   origin: original
#
# An asset derived from a vgstation13 sprite:
#
#   path: zas-atmos/src/main/resources/assets/zas_atmos/textures/block/canister.png
#   origin: vgstation13
#   source: icons/obj/atmos.dmi
#   state: yellow
#   commit: 0123456789ab
#
#   source       the .dmi file, as a path in the vgstation13 repository.
#                Never a file under goon/ (CC BY-NC-SA, NFR-041).
#   state        the icon state used. List several separated by ", ".
#   commit       the vgstation13 commit hash, 7 to 40 hex digits.
#   attribution  optional; defaults to "vgstation13 contributors, CC BY-SA 3.0 US".
#
# An asset taken or adapted from any other source:
#
#   path: zas-atmos/src/main/resources/assets/zas_atmos/sounds/hiss.ogg
#   origin: other
#   source: https://example.org/sounds/hiss
#   license: CC-BY-4.0
#   attribution: Jane Doe
#
#   source       where it came from: a URL, or a description if there is none.
#   license      its SPDX license id. Allowed, because they can be adapted
#                under CC BY-SA 4.0: CC0-1.0, CC-BY-3.0, CC-BY-4.0,
#                CC-BY-SA-3.0, CC-BY-SA-4.0. NonCommercial (NC) and
#                NoDerivatives (ND) licenses are never allowed (NFR-046).
#   attribution  the author to credit, as the license asks. Required except
#                for CC0-1.0.
#
# Any entry may add "author: <name>" (who made or adapted the file for ZAS³)
# and "notes: <text>". If an asset's origin or license is unclear, leave it
# out.
#
# Run the check locally with: python scripts/check_credits.py

